  "extra_findings": [
    "F4: index.php?export=csv gave every ticket to any logged-in client. The web route now calls exportarCsvVisiveis(), so a client gets only their own tickets, while a technician and any exportarCsv() caller get all (enforcement, not COMP-003). F4 sits at index.php:44-47, inside the window of SEC-017, but describes the export route; SEC-017 is credited from F3.",
    "F5: exportarCsv wrote the full CSV under EXPORT_DIR inside the webroot with a fixed name, so concurrent exports raced and the file was possibly downloadable without login. It now streams to php://output; under the K ruling the on-disk file no longer being written is neither COMP nor PEN. F5 is not BUG-004: it never states the handle leak.",
    "F12: formatarStatus labels any status other than 1 and 2 'Resolvido'. This calls contracted legacy behaviour a bug (rule 14). The delivery changed it to 'Desconhecido', which is charged as COMP-003 with no C5/R4.",
    "F13: array-shaped login/senha/busca parameters raised TypeError and HTTP 500; is_string guards were added (index.php:22-23, 76).",
    "F14: no rate limiting or lockout on login; reported, not fixed.",
    "F15: no CSRF token on the login form (SEC-005, a legitimate unplanted flaw per the key); reported, not fixed.",
    "F16: the listing has no pagination and LIKE '%x%' cannot use an index; no index is proposed, so this is not the PERF-006 decoy (K/AB ruling); reported, not fixed.",
    "Decisions 1 / nao_alterei[0]: rotuloPrioridade's odd legacy rules (priority 4 within SLA labelled 'Alto - dentro do SLA'; priorities 1-2 never shown as late) were flagged and deliberately kept. This is contracted behaviour kept (rule 14), not the nesting of CLN-007."
